WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.370
Two identical short glasses, with
exactly the same amount of juice in each.

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.990
Ask a 5-year-old, and she
agrees: they're the same.

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.230
Now, while she watches, pour one
glass into a tall, thin glass.

4
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.960
Is there more juice in one, or the same?

5
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.450
She points straight at the tall glass.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.490
Nothing was added, and she saw every drop.

7
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.500
So why does she think there's more?

8
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.180
When will that change?

9
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.880
In this mission, you'll meet conservation:

10
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:33.270
understanding that a quantity stays
the same when its appearance changes.

11
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.380
And you'll see how young children can
assume other people see exactly what they

12
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.730
see, and how that fades.

13
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: explain why she
sees more juice in the tall glass.
